			<div class="content" id="post-content-4208104">
									

<p>i really like this, got some line by line tone stuff coming in a second. i cleared your tags - don't tag stuff by yourself unless you know what you're doing, because you didn't have all the tags you needed and the tagging team looks for untagged articles.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Critique&nbsp;under&nbsp;here</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Your containment procedures are a little short, but honestly that's about all I could see this guy needing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>hitherto undiscovered substance with properties similar to rubber</p>
</blockquote>
<p>just take out the &quot;hitherto undiscovered&quot;, it's a goofy thing that a lot of people on the site don't like. we can assume this guy's rubber-stuff is anomalous, we don't need to know it's undiscovered.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 locomotes in a variety of ways, most of which appear to be poorly coordinated.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this sentence could be trimmed down - we really just need to know that he's got bad coordination. people locomote in a variety of ways.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ways that do not seem possible within the constraints of conventional physics</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this could probably just be &quot;ways that seem physically impossible&quot;, it also means you're not using &quot;conventional&quot; two sentences in a row.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;stuck&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>kill the scare quotes</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 appears to be sapient and is capable of at least somewhat coherent speech.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;is sapient and capable of speech&quot; (you talk about how he's incoherent right after this)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>to state that her four-year-old son, Jonathan, was missing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>maybe &quot;to report the disappearance of her four-year-old son, Jonathan&quot;? &quot;state&quot; is such a bland word</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Details given to the 911 dispatcher stated</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this sentence structure is weird - I would take out the first clause entirely, just say that Mrs. W told the dispatcher [facts].</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mrs. W████████, who had never been divorced or widowed, immediately became suspicious, and assumed that Jonathan had been kidnapped upon not finding him home.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>i mean if she's still married to the kid's dad she would probably assume he got kidnapped right away (also say that she's still married to the kid's dad, &quot;never divorced or widowed&quot; is a weird phrasing)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mrs. W████████, having never seen the alleged “stepdad”, was unable to give further details.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I assume the teacher would've been able to give some details? this sentence could probably just go.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>over 144 kilometers per hour</p>
</blockquote>
<p>someone converted 90mph to kilometers. round that bad boy up to 150 or down to 140.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>posing as FBI.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>he's not posing as the Whole FBI. &quot;an FBI agent&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>bobble around</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;bobble&quot; isn't super clinical but i can;t think of a good replacement so you could leave this one in</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the self-inflicted face slamming.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would just take this bit out, or put that he's uninjured up where he slams his face into the table</p>
<blockquote>
<p>involved in its regular pattern of manically stumbling around its cell and slamming into walls,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;involved in its pattern&quot; is a weird structure - maybe &quot;engaging in its usual behavior&quot; ?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>removing a pistol from under his pillow</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this is irresponsible, and super an action movie cliche. just have it in his nightstand drawer or something.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Researcher ███████ also requested the Foundation grant him a larger firearm for personal use. Request was denied.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>also this is super lolfoundation and wouldn't go in the containment documents regardless, i would take that out also</p>
<p>also i think you're a little heavy-handed on the redactions - you could definitely uncensor dates and some of the names.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>anyway i love this article and i think doing at least most of these edits would help it a lot - people get picky about tone, u know?</p>

