				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3938622); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3938622&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834506" alt="The Great Hippo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3938622)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-great-hippo" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3938622); return false;" >The Great Hippo</a></span> <span class="odate time_1557463337 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 May 2019 04:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4244123">
									

<p>So, I really like the energy, premise, and structure of this article. The execution&#8230; could use a <em>lot</em> of polishing. But all the stuff underneath that execution has a wild, frantic, terrifying energy that blends horror and comedy together really well.</p>
<p>A few things:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">CRITICISM</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 is a humanoid entity approximately 1.8m tall, resembling a middle-aged Caucasian male with the exception of a complete lack of any hair or genitalia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>'Caucasian' is, as a term, inaccurate; it refers to an obsolete taxon. No self-respecting scientist would use it unless they were referring to someone from the Caucasus. I also think you've got a great opener here, but you're over-doing it with details:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 is a white human male who lacks any hair, internal organs, or external genitalia.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 is composed entirely of a substance with properties similar to rubber. Both internal scans and attempts at physical dissection have indicated that SCP-4092’s body is a singular, solid piece of this material, lacking internal organs entirely.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 is composed of a substance similar to rubber. Its internal morphology is solid, lacking internal structure.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092's physical movements are bizarre and erratic, and at times seemingly inconsistent with the laws of conventional physics. On multiple occasions, SCP-4092 has been found apparently partially embedded within otherwise solid objects, unable to be removed from them via conventional means. However, SCP-4092 appears to have the ability to remove itself from this state without causing any perceivable damage to the object in which it was &quot;stuck&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092's movements are erratic and inconsistent with conventional physics. On multiple occasions, SCP-4092 has partially embedded itself into solid objects. It has demonstrated the ability to remove itself from these objects without damage to either itself or the object.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4092 appears to be sapient and is capable of speech.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This line isn't necessary. You <em>show</em> us he's sapient and capable of speech (in the logs), and there's no reason to presume he otherwise wouldn't be.</p>
<hr />
<p>Etc. There's a lot of redundancy here (don't say things 'appear to be' when they are, etc). A lot of language you could tighten up on.</p>
<p>The black-boxes are unnecessary; the logs feel like they could have a somewhat cleaner presentation, and there are several points where the visual descriptions in the logs felt more 'novel-esque' than they needed to be (and also similarly felt redundant).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><em>ALL</em> this being said: Holy shit, the premise (and the content of the logs themselves). The whole idea of connecting a step-dad's attempt to be wildly fun to their new kids with this magical entity who's behavior is terrifying and bizarre is a really great energy. I think the logs could have been tighter in a lot of places, but for the most part, they absolutely nail the concept &#8212; the logs are what got me to upvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
